    - id: 20
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: 'Sloth is typically associated with people who refuse to work or contribute
          to society.  That is something he plays on, but for the most part this
          association is a ruse.  '
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 20
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 24
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1030.6666
        y: 388.33325
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 24
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "He is more closely connected to the lack of empathy.  When a disaster
          happens - it is our job as people to help one another (as teaches the Holy
          Owl).  Tragically, some would rather ignore or cheer at the death of innocents
          if it means that they face one less problem of their own.  It is the inherent
          selfishness of apathy that this devil truly feeds on. Honing your own sense
          of passion and judgement is the best way to avoid this devil\u2019s grasp.\r\n\r\n"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 24
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 8
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1270.6666
        y: 421.6132
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 25
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: All devils know of their history and Greed is no exception.  All devils
          of sin are bound by the specificity of their contracts with mortals.  This
          means that Greed has to give the other party what they want, but that person
          must uphold their end of the deal as well. A broken contract can have terrible
          consequences for whomever breaks it.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 25
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 26
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1097.6653
        y: 478.24347
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 26
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: What the devil of Greed usually wants is his power restored, slaves
          returned, or an economic opportunity in which he can enrich himself.  Unfortunately,
          the rich talk with this devil a lot, but their souls and stories can tell
          what happen when you deal with him.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 26
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 8
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1270.0001
        y: 539.66656
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 27
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: A devil of ambition but also of loyalty to his masters. He is the
          strongest out of all of the sins and mainly used as a general.  He doesn't
          bother being manipulative like some of the others because he is content
          being a pawn for his masters. Pride doesn't need to think when stubbornly
          clinging to the wills of others.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 27
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 8
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 854.3216
        y: 649.55414
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 28
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: Some people are surprised to find the devil of Lust to be a man. 
          He is also the politest of the bunch and seems "kind" when someone first
          meets him.  However, out of any devil, make sure you never deal with him.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 28
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 31
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 632.6667
        y: 678.99994
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 31
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: 'Lust is a devil who embodies the greatest of human desires. He believes
          that all actions, at their roots, are a result of the truest human desire:
          power. The yearning for control, for power over another in the most complete
          way possible...  That is the embodiment of the Devil of Lust.  '
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 31
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 8
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 823.6918
        y: 762.8458
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 32
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: Devils of Sin don't really die. They usually reform in a chamber in
          the Depths. Depending on how recently Wrath has been recreated in the Depths,
          he might have a different perspective from the last time you knew of him.
          Typically, he switches between being bent on the destruction of all things,
          including hell, or pushing the idea of destruction on others. In the former,
          he often expresses hatred for the very concept of life. Regardless he is
          the devil that changes the most in philosophy and goals.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 32
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 8
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 391.95197
        y: 724.77216
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 33
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "Most people think Gluttony is about over-consumption of food, but
          over-consumption can apply to more. Thoughts of loneliness, fear, and revenge\u2026
          thought spirals that cycle through the mortal mind and encompass every
          waking thought. This devil supposedly gets \"attached\" to his prey quickly,
          offering companionship to those in need of it. Unfortunately, there are
          always strings attached to his outstretched hand."
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: 
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 33
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 8
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
